# ── Browser (this file) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project:
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#
# Both are safe in the browser bundle. The publishable/anon key is a public
# identifier, not a secret — row-level security is what protects the data.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# ── Edge Functions (NOT this file) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# These do not belong in .env.local. They live in Supabase's secret store and
# are read by the scheduled functions through Deno.env, never by the browser.
# Listed here only so there is one place that records what the jobs need.
#
#   npx supabase secrets set CRON_SECRET='<long random string>'
#   npx supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY='re_...'
#   npx supabase secrets set MORNING_MAIL_FROM='Margin <hello@yourdomain.com>'
#   npx supabase secrets set MORNING_MAIL_REPLY_TO='you@gmail.com'   # optional
#
# CRON_SECRET must match the value in the job_config table — see BACKEND.md.
# Without it both functions reject every call, so nothing is ever sent.
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the mail job runs and reports "skipped" rather than
# failing, so the rest of the schedule keeps working.
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected by the platform.
# Never set those yourself, and never prefix any of this with VITE_.
